        "id": "ch1_5_2-1",
        "text": "Linux OS Information\nKnowing the OS information for a Linux host is crucial for privilege escalation.\nThat\u2019s how you will know if the version used is vulnerable to privilege escala-\ntion (we will talk more about this topic in Chapter 10).\nTo display the operating system information of a Linux OS (which is Kali\nLinux in our case), I use the uname command, and along with it I display the\ncontents of the /etc/issue configuration file:\n$uname -a\n$cat /etc/issue\nroot@kali:/# uname -a\nLinux kali 5.6.0-kali2-amd64 #1 SMP Debian 5.6.14-2kali1 (2020-06-10)\nx86_64 GNU/Linux\nroot@kali:/# cat /etc/issue\nKali GNU/Linux Rolling \\n \\l",
